{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim","kind":"proposition","title":"Charge conjugation equals the bar involution on the characters of $H_3(q)$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-lepton-meson-torus-knot-dictionary"],"cites":["references/jones1987","references/wenzl1988c"],"tags":["charge-conjugation","bar-involution","CPT","lepton","meson","standard-representation","matter-antimatter"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ParticleInteractions.two_only_unit_squares","text":"c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.md","leanSource":"c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim\"></a><p><em>On the Iwahori--Hecke algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_3(q)</code>, with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_i^2 = h\\sigma_i + 1</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h = q - q^{-1}</code>, let charge conjugation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">C\\colon \\sigma_i \\mapsto \\sigma_i^{-1}</code> act on braid words and let the bar involution <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{bar}\\colon q \\mapsto q^{-1}</code> act on coefficients. For the two-dimensional irreducible representation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(2,1)</code> and every braid word <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta \\in B_3</code>,</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\chi^{(2,1)}\\bigl(C(\\beta)\\bigr)(q) = \\chi^{(2,1)}(\\beta)(q^{-1}).</code></pre>\n<p><em>The same identity holds for the one-dimensional characters of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n(q)</code> for every <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code>, since these send <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_i</code> to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> or to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-q^{-1}</code>. So <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">C = \\mathrm{bar}</code> holds on every irreducible character of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_3(q)</code>, not only on the one-dimensional ones.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"9.7.2","page":"b/prop-c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim","qa":{"counts":{"pass":97,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":20,"unknown":0,"stale":78},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CBar.trace_conj_eq_trace_bar","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
